</simplesect>
The <computeroutput>get_impl</computeroutput> function template serves as a fallback mechanism for value retrieval when the provided type does not implement a <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ac627271520bf2fe8a4c4774bcd9bf343" kindref="member">get()</ref></computeroutput> member function. It simply returns the first argument, discarding any additional parameters.</para>
<para>This approach ensures that both custom types (with a <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ac627271520bf2fe8a4c4774bcd9bf343" kindref="member">get()</ref></computeroutput> method) and standard types (without a <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ac627271520bf2fe8a4c4774bcd9bf343" kindref="member">get()</ref></computeroutput> method) are supported seamlessly within the framework&apos;s generic getter utilities.</para>
<para>All definitions are intended for internal use within the framework and are implemented in the <computeroutput>include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus</computeroutput> folder to maintain a structured and modular codebase. </para>
